019f2c3d-f394-7fe8-bbdb-e9137f8881eb	TEXT	\N	019f2c3d-f393-7148-b971-42512e808b26	To: All Warehouse Employees\nFrom: Paul Wandayi, Warehouse Manager\nDate: 15 March\nRe: New crates coming\n\nBeginning 1 April, Windquest Farms will use Flexmerge crates to transport our fruits and vegetables. These (131) ------- will simplify work and shrink operational costs.\n\nFlexmerge crates are collapsible, which means they are easy to stack and they save space. (132) ------- . They are also highly durable. This feature minimizes the need (133) ------- frequent replacement of crates. Finally, they are designed with ergonomic features, thereby (134) ------- the risk of injuries. Safety is our top priority here at Windquest Farms.
